# KSI-CNA-MAT: Azure Bastion - Secure Remote Access
# Validates Bastion host for secure management plane access

META
    esp_id `ksi-cna-mat-az-bastion-secure-access-001`
    version `1.0.0`
    dsl_schema_version `1.0.0`
    platform `azure`
    criticality `high`

    title `KSI-CNA-MAT: Azure Bastion - secure remote access without public IP`
    description `Validates that Azure Bastion is provisioned to provide secure RDP and SSH access to VMs without exposing public IP addresses, minimizing the attack surface`
    author `security-team`
    tags `azure,bastion,remote-access,ssh,rdp,attack-surface`

    control_mapping `KSI:KSI-CNA-MAT,KSI:KSI-CNA-RNT,NIST:AC-17,NIST:SC-7`
    control_objective `KSI-CNA-MAT`

    assessment_method `TEST`
    implementation_status `implemented`
    responsible_role `cloud-admin`

    control_origination `sp-system`
    customer_responsibility `configuration`

    remediation_days `7`
    recommendation `Deploy Azure Bastion in the hub VNet to provide secure browser-based RDP/SSH access, eliminating the need for public IPs on VMs`

    impl_KSI_CNA_MAT `Attack surface minimization is validated by confirming Azure Bastion is provisioned (found=true, provisioningState=Succeeded) to provide secure, browser-based RDP and SSH connectivity to virtual machines. Bastion eliminates the need for public IP addresses on VMs and removes direct internet-facing management ports (3389/22), reducing the attack surface. All management traffic flows through the Bastion service over TLS, providing audit logging and session recording capability.`

    impl_KSI_CNA_RNT `Network traffic restriction is enforced by Bastion proxying all management sessions through a hardened Azure-managed service, preventing direct inbound RDP/SSH connections to VM network interfaces.`

META_END

DEF
    OBJECT bastion_demo
        name `bas-example-prod`
        resource_group `rg-example-eastus`
    OBJECT_END

    STATE st_bastion_active
        found boolean = true
        provisioning_state string = `Succeeded`
    STATE_END

    CRI AND
        CTN az_bastion_host
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF st_bastion_active
            OBJECT_REF bastion_demo
        CTN_END
    CRI_END
DEF_END
